# Code owners — who must approve a pull request touching a given path.
#
# Purpose: the mobile app is developed by a contributor whose work is scoped to
# `mobile/`. An AI-assisted session on a mobile branch can still wander outside
# that directory, and `tasks.md` cannot prevent it — only review can. Every path
# below therefore requires the maintainer's explicit approval, so a stray edit to
# the platform cannot merge unnoticed.
#
# Requires "Require review from Code Owners" to be enabled in the branch
# protection rules for `main`. Without that setting this file is advisory only.
#
# NOTE: verify @tunavis is the correct GitHub username for the maintainer — a
# username that does not exist silently matches nobody, which fails open.

# Default: the maintainer owns everything not matched more specifically below.
*                       @tunavis

# The platform. Nothing in mobile work has any reason to touch these.
/api/                   @tunavis
/web/                   @tunavis
/processor/             @tunavis
/shared/                @tunavis
/db/                    @tunavis
/drivers/               @tunavis
/scripts/               @tunavis

# Main specs are the shared source of truth and are only ever written by
# archiving a change. A change proposes deltas inside its own
# `openspec/changes/` directory; it never edits these directly.
/openspec/specs/        @tunavis

# Infrastructure, CI, and the repo-wide guardrails.
/.github/               @tunavis
/docker-compose.yml     @tunavis
/docker-compose.*.yml   @tunavis
/nginx/                 @tunavis
/mosquitto/             @tunavis
/.gitignore             @tunavis
/CLAUDE.md              @tunavis
/openapi.json           @tunavis

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The contributor's own territory. Deliberately UNOWNED — a pattern with no
# owner after it removes ownership for that path, and GitHub takes the LAST
# matching pattern, so these must stay at the bottom of the file.
#
# Without these two lines the `*` default above swallows them, and the mobile
# app the contributor was hired to build would need the maintainer named as a
# code owner on every file in it. `tasks.md` tells him to tick a checkbox and
# open a PR after each task, so `rebuild-mobile-app/` is part of the work, not
# a spec he is reaching into: locking it makes his own progress log
# unwritable. Branch protection still requires one approving review on every
# PR — and nobody can approve their own — so the maintainer reads all of this
# regardless. What these lines remove is the second, redundant gate, not the
# review.
/mobile/
/openspec/changes/rebuild-mobile-app/
